 see that happen  unlike traditional zombies who are  driven entirely by instinct the alphas  and zombie king and army of the dead  appear to be up to something more  complex lily says she never figured out  exactly what the alpha zombies are doing  but we get a few  clues the first is that the people the  alphas capture are not immediately eaten  or turned by the zombies but are taken  to zeus to be turned into alphas this  suggests that he doesn't just want more  zombies in general but specifically more  alphas  the second is when we learn that zeus's  queen is pregnant although we have no  idea how two zombies were able to  conceive a child its inclusion points to  the idea that zeus is intentionally  building a zombie civilization  maybe he plans to eventually form an  actual army and venture out into the  world to conquer other civilizations and  bring them under his control  unfortunately for him las vegas gets hit  with a nuclear bomb wiping out the new  race he's creating before they can  attempt to expand beyond the walls of  the city  as ward's team pushes further into the  ruins of las vegas they come across the  remains of other teams that appear to  have been on the same mission  they deduce that this must not be the  first time that tanaka has hired a team  to recover his abandoned cash but the  other teams failed  at one point while examining the remains  of a team outside the save van der rohe  muses that the other teams are in fact  themselves caught in an infinite time  loop of death and failure  is this a hint that army of the dead  actually is some sort of macabre  tenant-like world of interwoven  timelines  well probably not most likely the other  teams were exactly that  other teams that died in pursuit of  their mission bandaro's comment is meant  more to draw attention to the  similarities between them and to  foreshadow their ultimate failure than  to imply that the other teams were  literally them  while ward and the rest of the team are  under the impression that the most  valuable thing in las vegas was the  giant pile of cash in the casino vault  martin knows better  his secret mission is to bring back the  head of a zombie for tanaka  giving his boss the ability to create  his very own army of the dead  the fact that martin is on board with  this plan speaks to his callousness  since he doesn't think twice about all  the people that zombie army could hurt  so it's not shocking that once he has  what he wants he doesn't hesitate to  betray his whole team and attempt to  leave them behind  eager to keep the spoils of the mission  all for himself ironically this lack of  basic human decency turns out to be his  downfall  since if he'd had some backup he may  have avoided becoming zombie tiger food  despite its disasters and you can't say  that ward didn't plan his heist well  his team is solid composed of himself  expert safecracker dieter helicopter  pilot marianne peters guide lilly his  trusted zombie war allies maria and van  der rohe  additional sharpshooters mikey and  chambers and tanaka's head of security  martin  at the last minute his daughter kate  strong arms her way onto the team and  lily recruits the deplorable cummings  cummings is the first to fall with lily  shooting him in the leg and leaving him  as a sacrifice for the zombies  he's turned into an alpha by zeus and  later killed by kate  chambers is next to go after being  abandoned in a zombie-packed building by  martin  although she fights valiantly and takes  out scores of the undead along with her  the rest make it into the vault where  they are betrayed and locked in by  martin  that decision comes back to bite him  literally when martin is then shredded  by a zombie tiger  as for the others maria gets her neck  snapped by zombies when they break into  the bank vault and mikey blows himself  up after getting bitten while trying to  escape  dieter holds his own for a while but  ultimately sacrifices himself to save  andero  shutting his friend in the safe as he's  swarmed by zombies lily provides a  distraction long enough for ward and  peters to escape on the helicopter only  to be rewarded for her trouble with a  pull through the chest  against all odds a few members of ward's  team do make it out of sin city although  some of them don't last very long  afterward either  van der rohe eventually climbs out of  the safe after their nuclear blast and  boards a plane to mexico  only to realize while in the air that  he's been infected by the zombie virus  as for ward he's bitten by zeus when the  zombie king leaps onto the helicopter  during their struggle peter peters is  shot in the shoulder impeding her  ability to fly  she does her best to stay airborne but  ultimately crashes in the desert and is  killed on impact  guido is also on board the helicopter  but we never see her after the crash  implying that she likely dies  kate is the only one who survives  relatively unscathed  ward gives her the small pile of cash  she's managed to hold on to but then  begins to transform into a zombie and is  shot in the head by a tearful kate  while they're successful in breaking  into the safe and locating the cash  ward's team is destined not to get very  far with it much of the money remains in  the save shut in with van der rohe until  the end of the film  the others try to take some money with  them at first but either abandon it or  are killed while holding it  most of the money either gets destroyed  in the bombing of las vegas or is  entombed forever in the safe  however wart does manage to pocket a  small stack of bills which isn't much  compared to the fortune in the safe but  is still likely somewhere around fifty  thousand dollars  he passes it to kate before he dies  telling her to use it to buy freedom for  gita's kids  and van der rohe makes it out with three  bags likely holding a few million which  he uses to charter a plane to mexico  city  unfortunately he realizes mid-flight  that he's been bitten meaning all that  cash isn't likely to do him much good  we never learn exactly why van der rohe  remained in the safe for so long after  dieter shut him in perhaps he passed out  or he was waiting until he could be sure  the zombies outside were gone or maybe  he was waiting for the nuclear blast  whatever his motivation for remaining in  the safe for a few hours it saves his  life  at least for a little while ironically  knowing that bandaro and his bags of  money could successfully weather a  nuclear blast inside that safe  it becomes clear that if tanaka's intent  really was to recover the money there  was no need to rush in before the city  was destroyed  he could have waited to send in a team  until after the strike when all the  zombies were dead  that really would have been the simple  in and out mission he pitched toward  all we know about tanaka is that he's a  billionaire who owns at least one casino  and who is famous enough that ward  recognizes him the minute he walks into  his diner  he says that insurance has already paid  out the money that was in the safe but  that he wants a cash anyway  however we later learned that the entire  scheme is a ruse to get martin into the  city in order to steal a zombie head so  tanaka can create more of them which  martin calls the ultimate weapon of mass  destruction  tanaka doesn't give about the money we  never learned what tanaka wanted an army  for  or whether he had any personal desire  for conquest at all  ramsay simply wanted to be in possession  of the world's greatest super weapon for  the purposes of power and profits and  didn't care what happened as a result  although army of the dead ends with las  vegas turned into a pile of rubble the  film does leave the door open for  zombies to remain in the world in any of  several ways  first there is the possibility that the  virus has already spread beyond the  borders of las vegas  the film doesn't give any hard evidence  of this but it's clear that the  government is concerned about it  additionally since we don't know where  zeus came from it's always possible  there might be more like him somewhere  else  but of course the strongest bit of  evidence that zombies still exist in the  world of army of the dead is the reveal  at the end of the film that van der rohe  was himself infected  of course there's always the possibility  that he could be killed or contained  while on the plane so that the virus  doesn't spread beyond him  but given the rest of the bad luck and  army of the dead the infection stopping  with van der rohe seems unlikely  plans have already been greenlit for an  army of the dead prequel and anime  series but we can't rule out the  possibility of a direct sequel either  despite the film's high body count  a sequel could continue vandaro's  open-ended storyline once his plane  lands in mexico  perhaps he becomes the new zombie king  or maybe he defies the odds yet again  and figures out how to stop his  infection from spreading this seems to  be the most clearly defined  path towards setting up a spin-off  storyline through an established  character  another option is following kate after  she frees gida's children from the  quarantine camps maybe she fulfills her  father's dream of opening a food truck  only to once again be pulled back into  the zombie wars  a sequel could also branch off onto a  new path entirely following a different  group of characters through a new zombie  outbreak  maybe what happens in vegas doesn't stay  in vegas after all  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite new movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

